1. What is the project?

CCI is a gamified Coca-Cola customer-engagement application.

The main idea is to encourage people to buy Coca-Cola products more frequently by turning purchases into an interactive game.

Instead of simply buying a Coca-Cola product and consuming it, the user can receive rewards from the purchase, use those rewards to customize a digital avatar, compete with friends, and participate in outfit battles.

The core loop is:

Buy Coca-Cola
      ↓
Scan/redeem purchase code
      ↓
Receive coins
      ↓
Spend coins on digital clothing/items
      ↓
Customize avatar
      ↓
Challenge friends
      ↓
Compete in outfit battles
      ↓
Followers vote
      ↓
Winner receives prize pool
      ↓
Winning streak increases
      ↓
User continues participating
      ↓
More engagement with Coca-Cola

The business goal is not simply to create a game. The game is a marketing mechanism intended to increase Coca-Cola product purchases, engagement, and customer retention.

2. Current development strategy

We originally planned to build the complete product as a mobile application using Flutter.

However, there is a Coca-Cola event called Cola Fest, where we want to test the concept earlier.

Building and distributing the full mobile application would take significantly more time, so we are considering:

Telegram Bot
      +
Telegram Mini App
      +
FastAPI backend
      +
PostgreSQL

for the Cola Fest MVP.

The Telegram Bot will primarily handle communication and notifications, while the Mini App will contain the actual game/application interface.

Eventually, the full product can become:

Flutter mobile app
        +
FastAPI backend
        +
PostgreSQL

The important point is that the backend/business logic should be reusable.

