20. Business logic vs database models

One important architectural principle for the project:

Models describe data.

For example:

Competition

describes what information a competition contains.

Services implement business rules.

For example:

accept_competition_request()

could:

verify that the request is pending
verify that the participants aren't already in active competitions
create the competition
mark the request accepted
cancel conflicting pending requests
send a notification

Routers expose the functionality through HTTP.

POST /competition-requests/{id}/accept

So the general flow is:

Mini App
   ↓
HTTP request
   ↓
FastAPI router
   ↓
Service / business logic
   ↓
SQLAlchemy
   ↓
PostgreSQL


